# XSH quick_exit()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Each test forks a child that registers handlers with at_quick_exit() and
# ends with quick_exit(); the handlers report with write() on a pipe and the
# parent judges the report and the wait status.

assertion  XSH.quick_exit.001
anchor     functions/quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       quick_exit() calls the functions registered with at_quick_exit()
           in the reverse order of registration (three handlers registered
           1, 2, 3 run 3, 2, 1) and the process then ends.
test       t/001-reverse-order.c

assertion  XSH.quick_exit.002
anchor     functions/quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       quick_exit() does not call functions registered with atexit().
test       t/002-not-atexit.c

assertion  XSH.quick_exit.003
anchor     functions/quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       The process ends as if by _Exit(status): the wait status shows a
           normal exit with the status given, for 0, 1, 42 and 255, with
           and without registered functions.
test       t/003-status.c

assertion  XSH.quick_exit.004
anchor     functions/quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       If a registered function does not return (it calls _exit()), the
           functions still to run are not called and the termination is not
           completed otherwise: the wait status is the one the function
           gave.
test       t/004-handler-no-return.c

assertion  XSH.quick_exit.005
anchor     functions/quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A function registered while quick_exit() is running (when the
           registration succeeds) is called after the function that
           registered it and before the functions that were registered
           earlier than that one: registrations 1, 2, with 2 registering 3,
           give the order 2, 3, 1.
note       Whether such a late registration succeeds is unspecified; if it
           fails the test is NOTINUSE.
test       t/005-register-in-handler.c

assertion  XSH.quick_exit.006
anchor     functions/quick_exit.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       Each registered function is called exactly once, also when the
           same function is registered several times (registered three
           times it runs three times).
test       t/006-once-each.c
